summary: A manifold whose reference measure is finite has a uniform distribution, with the constant density one over its mass; in a full chart its tangent coordinate has the chart's volume as its density, a Student t for the usual charts of the rotations and the spheres, so it is a mixture of normals over their scales; and no single normal approaches it, since a normal's mass leaves every compact part of a global chart as its scale grows.
depends_on: [chart-volume, normal]
---

<script>
	import Statement from '$lib/components/Statement.svelte';
	import Proof from '$lib/components/Proof.svelte';
	import * as tangent from './statements/tangent.md';
